For getComputedStyle(), Ladybird resolves the insets and margins of a
table from its table wrapper, and Blink, WebKit and Gecko all report the
same values. Gecko reads them from its separate wrapper frame, the
element’s primary frame, in nsComputedDOMStyle::GetUsedAbsoluteOffset()
and GetMarginFor(). Blink and WebKit have no separate wrapper object:
Blink’s LayoutTable produces the wrapper fragment, whose insets
ComputedStyleUtils::ValueForPositionOffset() reads, while WebKit’s
RenderTable carries the wrapper’s positioning and used margins itself.
